    completed_phase_gate: ADR-001 through ADR-010 are accepted in `docs/architecture/adr/`; they freeze metadata grammar, SHA-256/Merkle identity, alignment/layout, companion transport, browser persistence, quantization profiles, WebGPU support, specialist composition, service-worker release behavior, and evidence signing.
    completed_contract_increment: `tinyrustlm/tools/strict-json.js` now provides bounded fatal-UTF-8 duplicate-aware parsing, and all three release-authorization files pass through it before schema or Ed25519 verification. The verifier tool hash binds both modules and identifies profile `tinyrustlm.strict-json.v1`; hostile tests cover literal/escaped/supplementary duplicate names, invalid UTF-8, BOMs, lone surrogates, depth/entry/string limits, unsafe numbers, negative zero, overflow/underflow, malformed grammar, and trailing data.
    completed_contract_inventory: `docs/architecture/vnext-contract-inventory.md` records 215 dated schema IDs across 109 app/tool files, the canonical sorted-list SHA-256 `581eee525ee30f195f0a21cd71db8d60ff275866d51cb2d236df74f638bd6d10`, 166 `JSON.parse` calls across 77 files, class-by-class ownership/gaps/deletion disposition, and exactly nine incompatible `tinyrustlm.vnext.*` family names. Every dated schema is historical-only and no alias, migration, or fallback authority exists.
    completed_contract_freeze: `contracts/vnext/contract-family.v1.json` is the single 37,361-byte frozen registry for the nine incompatible schema families; SHA-256 is `432188d01b5ad7c7cd535d7df4924627ec288eb8be15c251e09dd949ed767818`. It closes every object, rejects unknown fields, fixes parser/resource and semantic lifetime budgets, declares exact per-contract identity derivation and exclusions, uses private-by-default visibility, defines acyclic public-safe redaction, gives role-separated signing/registry/revocation/offline-bundle payloads explicit fields, preserves context provenance and precedence, binds worker/companion direction and state, recomputes P2P piece/Merkle facts, binds claims to site/route/component/source/release/owner, and has no extension, legacy, migration, fallback, alias, or dated-schema acceptance field.
    completed_validator_checkpoint: `contracts/vnext/contract-corpus.v1.json` is a deterministic 122,628-byte language-neutral raw-byte corpus with SHA-256 `d0eaf1dc0295c21877581381120649d744ec0ba2cd5d9495fabdc293083889e7`; it binds registry SHA-256 `432188d01b5ad7c7cd535d7df4924627ec288eb8be15c251e09dd949ed767818` and normalized generator SHA-256 `bbe300a6678dae17c247ff1cacbb3f2f5467fc71757df91642c5885c1108b9fe`. It has 69 cases, 14 accepts and 55 rejects. The registry interpreter (`d60d9b86be75e9cb17b81b043baabf19d74de80dadb23241d733bec6261ceabc`) and separately written independent validator (`607f1986e8acaa14c877860d317dde87900870964dbb2415b07f7b11eccceaba`) agree with all expected verdicts for 138 differential executions. Property checks cover arbitrary key order, every root required-field deletion, and unknown-field injection at every reachable object depth. Only the registry interpreter exposes checked/not-applicable/deferred invariant accounting; the independent implementation is a separately sourced verdict oracle.
    completed_phase_2_threat_review: `docs/architecture/vnext-contract-threat-review.md`, 14,555 bytes, SHA-256 `c799b6112b677cb3c6ed75d25da4cb59cc1f9b69c9c4eaa0d57406f1972b1893`, records PASS for the Phase 2 schema-and-local-invariant boundary only. It explicitly does not grant production cutover, cryptographic evidence, model quality, browser round, live memory, public P2P, catalog, package, site, or campaign authority.
    remaining_contract_risk: Full RFC 8785 cross-language identity vectors, domain-separated hash recomputation, Ed25519 verification, key authority/role/time/registry/revocation enforcement, receipt-DAG closure and invalidation, offline-bundle closure, bounded secret/redaction execution, atomic durable persistence, bounded streaming, Rust/browser/WASM parity, production entry-point cutover, and deletion of superseded readers/writers remain incomplete. Existing dated evidence remains historical and cannot satisfy vNext gates.
    exact_next_action: Start with failing RFC 8785/JCS and receipt-identity tests that reproduce the current option-boundary defect. Freeze canonical and domain-separated identity vectors, repair the canonicalizer call with an exact JCS-only limit object, and freeze one incompatible content-addressed receipt-store API. Then implement same-directory create-only atomic persistence with bounded streaming hashes, parent-DAG closure/cycle checks, role-bound Ed25519 verification, authority registry and revocation-time evaluation, offline-bundle closure, redaction-scan binding, startup quarantine, interruption/disk-full tests, and exact phase invalidation. Delete superseded production parsers only after every replacement entry point is verified; add no compatibility shim.
    no_compatibility_shims: SLM2 and the vNext schema family are intentionally incompatible clean contracts. Do not retain SLM1 fallback, old aliases, dual readers/writers, conversion-kit downloads, or user-run handoff scripts in the new product path.
