  related_site_account:
    inventory_scope: Direct site roots under `E:\Source\Rust`; local/remote source facts and the previously bounded public observations were reconciled into `E:\Source\Rust\workspace.uai` profile `rust-site-family.workspace.v7` on 2026-08-09. A live response, source commit, package version, HTTP Last-Modified value, and immutable publication receipt are different evidence classes and are labeled separately below.
    LMComposer.com: Retired alias. The local root is empty and has no Git repository; production responds with a redirect to TinyRustLM.com. Last publication is unknown because no immutable site release ledger exists.
    MiniModel.MiRust.com: Active MiniModel developer documentation. Local commit `3c5f9e28c48fd2b843f58df91accc5579a3270a5` is clean and equals the remote branch; the observed live root was byte-identical to local and returned Last-Modified `2026-07-12T22:33:49Z`. This HTTP metadata is not an immutable publication receipt.
    MiniModel.org: Active public catalog and direct-P2P discovery surface; it must never proxy model bytes. Local commit `693c50f0fa2a82fd502dfc9d38c0e140531850da` is clean and equals the remote branch; the observed live root was byte-identical to local and returned Last-Modified `2026-07-14T07:33:16Z`. No immutable site release ledger exists.
    MiRust.com: Active marketing, architecture, research, and governance site. Local commit `6dd665033c1d3a8ef907ee3140707a6fcb4c0357` is clean and equals the remote branch. The live footer reports latest content update `2026-06-25T16:42:00Z` and Theme/Core `2.3.0`; the local repository is not a complete independently verifiable WordPress deployment snapshot, and no immutable site release ledger exists.
    Runtime.MiRust.com: Retired route-aware compatibility site redirecting to `https://tinyrustlm.mirust.com/developer-portal/`. Local commit `3bf5a5de50d21c4a10e8dd08dffa1eabd83199fc` is clean and equals the remote branch; local `version.json` identifies package `1.1.0`, updated `2026-07-12T21:30:00Z`. No immutable site release ledger exists.
    TinyRustLM.com: Active browser-local product surface. The current immutable ledger records `tinyrustlm.com@0.2.1`, release date `2026-08-08`, published `2026-08-08T23:47:22.420Z`, source revision `e964a095ede1c077b36b6476af5ee85b087f52f8`, and publication ID `aea1e08b74f6b7835473ffb482baeddd42c97346d0a08868a66574f1a5d089ce`. The source revision is contained in the pushed active branch. This proves that bounded site publication only; it does not prove the enterprise campaign.
    TinyRustLM.MiRust.com: Active architecture and developer portal. Local/live identity is `1.6.0`, updated `2026-07-12T22:00:00Z`; local and GitHub remote are both commit `c9cd240221c6ff6efd7ab5fcc476dad96f75ad01`. A prior local remote-tracking reflog permission failure can make `git status` falsely report two unpushed commits, so use `git ls-remote` as the remote fact. No immutable site release ledger exists.
  publication_discipline:
    - Publish stable, coherent increments frequently, but never trade quality, security, evidence, or synchronized documentation for cadence.
    - Before each site publish, assign an intentional semantic version and release date, update a human-readable update log plus an immutable machine-readable release ledger, bind the exact clean source revision and artifact hashes, run relevant tests and secret scans, and obtain publication authorization.
    - Commit and push every affected source, documentation, marketing, and release-log repository before claiming publication. Deploy only from its source-control truth, then verify public HTTPS readback, version, release date, update log, asset hashes, and behavior.
    - Keep TinyRustLM.com, TinyRustLM.MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, MiniModel.MiRust.com, MiRust.com, and any retained redirect surfaces behaviorally and editorially consistent. Record an explicit blocker when a site cannot be updated; never call local files, package creation, upload attempts, or stale pages deployed.
    - Bring every retained active site onto one consistent immutable release-ledger contract; TinyRustLM.com is currently the only site in this inventory with `uaix.site_release.v1` publication evidence.
version_authority:
  current_version: 0.2.1
  next_version: 0.2.2
  policy: Increment intentionally after real implementation milestones; source scaffolding does not imply runtime support.
active_product:
  name: TinyRustLM
  root: tinyrustlm/
  purpose: Zero-dependency Rust/WASM browser-local SLM runtime and UI.
  enterprise_vnext_development_goal_2026_08_01: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-enterprise-vnext-development-goal-memory-2026-08-01.md`, SHA256 `22838f84d8df1b7daef4577fa5f52fdbcf31e7f20eeeb377bf2b6f092c5b5731`, routes the 25-report enterprise vNext synthesis and active 60,899-byte execution assignment, SHA256 `629d7bee195f80c4acb868ed90c4124fd80d2cf6a1060a8fe13fdaa65968b31a`. It requires clean incompatible contracts, ten ADR gates, scalar-first conformance, bounded browser/runtime/security/release work, champion-plus-sealed-specialists, immutable evidence, and synchronized sites. The reports are advisory and every 20/50/25/40/20 campaign counter remains unearned until objective receipts exist.
  pre_release_no_debt_authority_2026_07_15: TinyRustLM is not a live released product. Until the human explicitly removes this rule, add no technical debt, legacy support, backward-compatibility paths, dual contracts, migration shims, deprecated aliases, or knowingly temporary architecture. Clean replacement, deletion of superseded implementation after verification, and full rewrites are authorized. Immutable receipts and dated failure evidence remain historical truth, not supported product behavior. This authority supersedes incompatible present-tense wording in older dated workspace entries.
  model_acquisition_v2_authority_2026_08_08: The current acquisition contract supersedes older conversion-kit and import-kit workflow entries. One user action selects a model. A complete identity-matched MiniModel P2P offer with its composition graph is preferred and is imported through the paired local companion; otherwise, after explicit companion pairing, protocol v2 performs immutable reviewed Hugging Face source download, bounded resumable hashing, Rust conversion, Rust receipt reinspection, `.slm` validation, base-only `.acg1` creation, composition reinspection, direct loopback streaming, and browser activation. Progress and typed failures stay in the app. Model acquisition and P2P sharing must not download README/TXT, shell, PowerShell, request JSON, conversion-kit, share-kit, or serving-helper files and must not require users to run scripts. TinyRustLM.com, MiniModel.org, UAIX.org, and MemoryEndpoints.com receive no prompts, responses, source tensors, model bytes, or composition bytes. Browser-only local `.slm` import remains valid; companion access is explicit, scoped, session-bound, and never probed before consent. The packaged companion and Rust converter are version 0.2.0 for this contract; release and public-deployment claims remain pending objective gates.
  third_party_review_storage_authority_2026_07_21: Keep all downloaded third-party repositories, packages, papers, standards, source archives, and model-review inputs outside project repositories and Git under `E:\Source\external\{project-name}`. Source control may contain original TinyRustLM work plus public-safe URLs, immutable revisions, byte counts, hashes, licenses, and bounded findings, but not copied third-party review trees or machine-local external paths.
  source_control_model_payload_boundary_2026_07_26: Current source control contains no candidate, trained, converted, product, source-checkpoint, raw-tensor, or P2P-piece model payloads. Only six explicitly allowlisted deterministic `.slm` fixtures of at most 64 KiB remain, and they are runtime/test evidence only. Browser boot has no built-in model and requires admitted local, selector-registry, companion, or P2P intake. A preservation-only external manifest with SHA256 `96795962727efcae9ee142ba31a4de7b8d891e176ef6373a6a518383e2155bca` reverified 6 `.slm` artifacts plus 8 source checkpoints, 16,259,130,576 total bytes, and zero partial files; it grants no quality, release, catalog, or campaign-counter authority. Older entries naming tracked model paths or bootstrap selectors are immutable history, not current product behavior.
  exact_flat_named_target_performance_2026_07_22: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-named-target-performance-memory-2026-07-22.md`, SHA256 `20620ef887db16098a3d7de942c101653fba77aee06cb1951f9c3a4e23e71a68`, routes preregistration SHA256 `269459766b1bab57ce86cadda296d0941d3dfc3d6876873ab48657ba7bd64c63`, preserved pre-execution failure `exact-flat-physical-target-attempt-1291be20cc291bc6`, observation `exact-flat-physical-target-20bfb3e18230f257`, and child receipt `exact-flat-physical-target-verification-6b478318ef8747cb` file SHA256 `4cf29cef23b057677e97ed0e03751bac6ad88d31fe44dff2d93582c22d437c1e`. Three preregistered workloads and 324 retained query samples verify latency, throughput, and process memory only on the named Windows host. Energy, independent chassis attestation, complete physical-target status, sealed-corpus quality, crash-recovered deletion, compression, product, training, and release remain false. Never rerun either physical-target `--write` command.
  exact_flat_browser_wasm_verification_2026_07_21: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-browser-wasm-verification-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `b9191b867784c8c0323c8f2b484aca5c13c95a5766686a3da061cb35d83150a7`, routes v2 preregistration, committed runner, immutable observation `exact-flat-browser-wasm-0361d72f245abbd3` file SHA256 `d28c921ec1df7db538417aaed8803fce88bc6d37b3cbc5fcf5d291b0a91a6f9a`, and child receipt `exact-flat-browser-wasm-verification-8fcdeb0b93534ca4` file SHA256 `5c52a2287390f79e6a4971da6a6455a69c4ebd52ac6473bcce5408fd62560157`. The exact three-module, 49-test set ran in two real Chromium processes; all entry points returned zero, processes closed, unique profiles were deleted, and page-network/error counters were zero. This grants only exact experiment real-browser execution; use the newer named-target route for bounded host measurements. Sealed-corpus quality, durable deletion, compression, TurboVec parity, product, training, and release remain unproved. Never rerun either browser `--write` command.
  colibri_public_source_pin_2026_07_21: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-colibri-public-source-pin-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `3b3b36e1eb9daa8d4bb12787e20fed23e34559b2bfff58a640d0d9b213ac78fd`, routes direct review of public Colibri commit `44e489b196c9b7876b3d37a0570ebf1c6f90f54c`, tree `faae3d9594319ab856a4c3dd3f69a3afdd71f348`, and Apache-2.0 license. Default placement retains the full trained expert set on disk while changing residency; optional `CACHE_ROUTE=1` may change expert choice and needs its own quality gate. No upstream source entered TinyRustLM, and no compatibility, dependency, model-byte reduction, performance, quality, or adoption claim is authorized.
  exact_flat_retrieval_foundation_2026_07_21: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-retrieval-foundation-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `6a0f3241253b1d666959984869c4ec29eb04c97fb67a446ccdb89bc26423de76`, routes the preregistered dependency-free exact f32 baseline. Preregistration SHA256 is `0d9b6b3d31a25cba843034ceeafca3a88bc1287546f66025b62d13ba14441152`; ledger SHA256 is `7daa7653222914a028e636e6de6e195f94cb5eb50d5bd10a76af624877303808`; receipt `exact-flat-retrieval-75f95baa316315ea` SHA256 is `893e96f461f701f46a3aaaeecddd67bc2b700625ccdb9f0d83ce4b0b67d8c18c`. Checked scalar search, persistence, corruption detection, deletion/compaction, native tests, and WASM compilation pass; separate browser and named-target children close exact module execution and bounded host measurements. Coverage, Miri, representative-corpus quality, and crash-recovered on-disk deletion remain open; no TurboVec parity, compression, product, training, or release authority exists.
  current_local_import_and_p2p_authority_2026_07_15: Local picker input is bounded to 1 GiB, read in 4 MiB slices into one exact final WASM allocation, and finalized through Rust-owned incremental SHA-256 and TinyRustLM checksum state before runtime adoption. Conversion and local share kits may create peer pieces, a peer-free base catalog, and consenting local companion/contact handoffs, but they cannot create public availability. Public announcement requires MiniModel `prepare-seed-announcement` with an external probe receipt, observer trust configuration, and seed fleet configuration. The only current deep conversion modes are `hf-conversion-kit-safetensors-exec`, `hf-conversion-kit-review-exec`, `hf-conversion-kit-review-reject-exec`, `hf-conversion-kit-gguf-exec`, and `hf-p2p-import-kit-exec`; the former aggregate mode is deleted. Loopback and mapped-host tests remain local evidence and never count as outside-network proof or a live-release claim.
